...@_brand.d2

# Fig 0 — the idea in one picture. Deliberately not a wiring diagram: it states the
# claim (a face driven by *incremental* dialogue reacts during your turn, not after it)
# and leaves every mechanism to Figs 1-4.

direction: down

(** -> **)[*].style.stroke: "#555555"

user: You\nspeaking { class: neutral; shape: person }

signals: Incremental dialogue signals\nretico\n\nWHILE you speak — turn-taking, backchannel, nod\nAS words firm up — transcript revised, ADD / REVOKE / COMMIT\nAS the reply forms — clauses and affect, streamed { class: primary; style.font-size: 18 }

bridge: One protocol\n\nevery signal crosses the wire\nwith its incremental semantics intact { class: secondary; style.font-size: 18 }

face: Expressive face\nVizij · WASM rig in the browser\n\ngaze · blink · head nods\nexpression · lip-sync { class: primary; style.font-size: 18 }

user -> signals: 16 kHz audio,\ncontinuously
signals -> bridge
bridge -> face

face -> user: the face responds\nDURING your turn,\nnot after it { style: { stroke: "#EC4D00"; stroke-width: 3; font-color: "#EC4D00"; font-size: 19 } }

swap: Any stage swaps models at runtime — ASR · LLM · TTS, local or cloud { class: highlight; style.font-size: 16; near: bottom-center }
